# Combat Move Quick Reference

Lookup tables for the `POD_init_combat_move` constructor and its
`POD_combat_move_set_*` setters.

| You want | Read instead |
|---|---|
| Authoring workflow, balance guidance and system extensions | `COMBAT_MOVE_AUTHORING_GUIDE.info` |
| How the engine executes a move | `COMBAT_REFERENCE.info` |

A move is a `POD_combat_move` story owned by `character:POD_wraith_01`.
Setters define its attributes; omit optional setters for unused behaviour.
Presence flags have no "off" value.

Unknown variable names and values can have no effect without an error. See
section 20 for common failures.

---

## 1. What a move is made of

A move requires the following records and a catalogue version increment.

| Record | Where |
|---|---|
| Registry entry: constructor + setter block | `common/scripted_effects/POD_combat/pod_combat_move_list_effects.txt` |
| Shared unlock rule `pod_combat_move_<key>_unlock_trigger` | `common/scripted_triggers/POD_combat/pod_combat_move_unlock_triggers.txt` |
| Unlock switch case `flag:<key>` under the matching `CONFIG` branch | same file, in `pod_combat_actor_unlocks_move_trigger` |
| Hidden decision `POD_combat_move_<key>` (art + unmet-requirement text) | `common/decisions/POD_Combat/pod_combat_move_decisions.txt` |
| Three loc keys: name, `_desc`, `_tooltip` | `localization/english/gui/POD_combat_moves_l_english.yml` |
| `POD_current_combat_version` incremented once | `common/script_values/pod_combat_values.txt` |

```paradox
POD_init_combat_move = {
    DECISION   = POD_combat_move_your_key
    SKILL_KEY  = your_key
    CATEGORY   = ATK
    CONFIG     = your_section
    GROUP      = vampire
    AP_COST    = @ap_cost_medium
    AI_WEIGHT  = 20
    TARGETING  = single_enemy
}
scope:new_combat_move = {
    POD_combat_move_set_flag = { NAME = checks_guard }
    POD_combat_move_set_hp_damage = { VALUE = @damage_minor }
}
```

**Keep `scope:new_combat_move` immediately after its constructor.** Each
constructor replaces that saved scope, so a separated setter block applies to
the wrong move.

Both unlock switches fall back permissively. A missing switch case or a misspelled
`CONFIG` silently makes a restricted move available to everyone at runtime,
while its decision still shows the intended requirement. Every move needs an
explicit switch case, including a universal one whose rule is `always = yes`.

---

## 2. Constructor parameters

All eight are required.

| Parameter | Values |
|---|---|
| `DECISION` | `POD_combat_move_<key>`, matching the hidden decision |
| `SKILL_KEY` | unique lower-snake-case identifier; permanent, saved loadout presets store it |
| `CATEGORY` | `ATK`, `DEF`, `CTL`, `PWR` |
| `CONFIG` | the unlock switch case key (a discipline / section key, e.g. `base_physical`) |
| `GROUP` | `universal`, `vampire`, `werewolf`, `bastet`, `mokole`, `fera`, `fae`, `demon`, `wraith`, `mummy`, `kueijin`, `hunter`, `sorcerer`, `psychic`, `theurgy`, `truefaith` |
| `AP_COST` | integer, or an AP constant |
| `AI_WEIGHT` | integer base AI score |
| `TARGETING` | see section 7 |

`GROUP` only drives the loadout editor's "show all moves" display filter. It is
**never** an access gate; access lives entirely in the unlock trigger.

`CATEGORY` is not the AI's tactical intent. The AI infers intent from the
payload the move actually carries.

Conventional `AI_WEIGHT` by category, before tactical modifiers: ATK 20,
PWR 12, CTL 10, DEF 8.

