## 3. Resource costs

Set AP in the constructor; use setters for other costs.

```paradox
POD_combat_move_set_energy_cost   = { VALUE = @energy_cost_minor }
POD_combat_move_set_stress_cost   = { VALUE = @stress_cost_minor }
POD_combat_move_set_gold_cost     = { VALUE = @gold_cost_minor }
POD_combat_move_set_piety_cost    = { VALUE = @piety_cost_minor }
POD_combat_move_set_prestige_cost = { VALUE = @prestige_cost_minor }
```

| Family | Constants |
|---|---|
| AP | `@ap_cost_tiny` 1, `_minor` 2, `_medium` 3, `_major` 4, `_massive` 5, `_maximum` 6 |
| Energy | `@energy_cost_tiny` 1 .. `_maximum` 6, then `_seven` 7, `_eight` 8, `_nine` 9, `_ten` 10 |
| Stress | `@stress_cost_minor` 10, `_medium` 20, `_major` 40, `_massive` 80 |
| Gold | `@gold_cost_minor` 15, `_medium` 50, `_major` 150, `_massive` 500 |
| Piety | `@piety_cost_minor` 50, `_medium` 100, `_major` 250, `_massive` 500 |
| Prestige | `@prestige_cost_minor` 50, `_medium` 100, `_major` 250, `_massive` 500 |

Energy costs use the actor's splat energy pool. The unlock rule must ensure
the actor has one. Cost previews use `PODCombatMoveEnergyCost`: the full listed
cost is converted and rounded up for the living control-slot combatant during
active combat, or the viewer otherwise. Previews include encounter Dharma discounts
outside duels; actual spending requires `pod_combat_duel_active` for the
discount. Energy gains use their own conversion without the cost discount.

Stress, gold, piety and prestige are **paid by the player only**. Energy is
paid by the AI too. A player-only cost is not by itself balance for AI access.

