## 4. Damage and healing

```paradox
POD_combat_move_set_hp_damage    = { VALUE = @damage_minor }
POD_combat_move_set_morale_damage = { VALUE = @morale_damage_minor }
POD_combat_move_set_self_damage  = { VALUE = @self_damage_tiny }
POD_combat_move_set_hp_heal      = { VALUE = @healing_minor TYPE = superficial }
POD_combat_move_set_morale_heal  = { VALUE = @morale_heal_minor }
POD_combat_move_set_energy_gain  = { VALUE = 2 }
```

| Family | Constants |
|---|---|
| HP damage | `@damage_tiny` 1 .. `@damage_maximum` 6 |
| Morale damage | `@morale_damage_tiny` 1 .. `_maximum` 6 |
| Self-damage | `@self_damage_tiny` 1, `_minor` 2, `_medium` 3 |
| HP heal | `@healing_tiny` 1 .. `@healing_massive` 5 |
| Morale heal | `@morale_heal_tiny` 1 .. `_massive` 5 |

`set_hp_heal` takes `TYPE = superficial` or `TYPE = aggravated`. Aggravated
healing also reduces aggravated damage. Heal type is independent of damage
class.

`set_energy_gain` takes a number on the 0-10 energy scale. It restores the
actor's pool regardless of targeting and sums with fulfilled `energy_gain`
clauses before applying.

Morale damage has its own auto-hit path: no hit roll, no guard, no soak. It
still respects dodge and stealth.

Self-damage is always superficial and lands on the actor.

---

## 5. Damage class

```paradox
POD_combat_move_set_hp_damage    = { VALUE = @damage_minor }
POD_combat_move_set_damage_class = { VALUE = fire }
```

**Call the class setter after `set_hp_damage`,** which sets
`damage_type = superficial` and overwrites any earlier class.

| Value | Behaviour |
|---|---|
| `superficial` | Default from `set_hp_damage`; omit the class setter. |
| `aggravated` | Forced aggravated against every target, `REASON = duel_aggravated`. |
| `fire` | Always aggravated against every splat. |
| `lightning` | Always aggravated against every splat. |
| `balefire` | Always aggravated, plus a balefire health modifier stack per point of final damage. |
| `cold`, `sun`, `silver`, `gold`, `holy`, `poison`, `cold_iron` | Aggravated only against their matrix splats; some splats are immune. |

The move has one base class. Its `REASON` selects PoD's immunity, downgrade
and splat multipliers per target.

Aggravated damage is unsoakable without a bane modifier. `aggravated`, `fire`,
`lightning` and `balefire` bypass ordinary soak against every splat; other
classes do so against their matrix splats.

The class is consumed by a direct HP hit, a typed HP counter, a typed HP DoT,
or a `dot` bonus effect. On a move with none of those it is inert.

