## 6. Delivery capability flags

Four presence flags control offensive delivery.

```paradox
POD_combat_move_set_flag = { NAME = requires_hit_roll }
```

| Flag | Present means |
|---|---|
| `requires_hit_roll` | the attack rolls to hit and can miss |
| `checks_guard` | the target's Guard can block it, and is consumed |
| `checks_stance` | Dodge and Stealth can evade it |
| `checks_spirit_gate` | the physical spirit-contact gate applies (passes harmlessly through incorporeal targets unless the actor can damage spirits) |

Omit `checks_guard` to bypass Guard.

Common idioms:

| Idiom | Flags |
|---|---|
| Ordinary physical strike | all four |
| Supernatural blast | `checks_stance` only (auto-hits, ignores guard, reaches spirits) |
| Direct morale attack | `checks_stance` only |
| Contact-based control | `requires_control_contact` + the delivery flags it should respect |
| Guaranteed control | no delivery flags, no `requires_control_contact` |

`requires_control_contact` makes a move with no HP or morale payload missable:
a failed delivery suppresses its debuff tiers, **its buff tiers**, mind
control, and the AP-drain and initiative-debuff mirrors. Stances are applied
regardless. Omit it when the utility effect is meant to be guaranteed.

It is only meaningful on `single_enemy`. Team debuffs and stance strips
broadcast before the one-workspace contact check, so a team move cannot make
every recipient pass contact.

These flags remove stances, even without `checks_stance`:

| Flag | Effect |
|---|---|
| `bypass_dodge` | strip the target's Dodge, then ignore it |
| `bypass_stealth` | break the target's Stealth, then ignore it |

