## 7. `TARGETING`

| Value | Hits |
|---|---|
| `single_enemy` | one selected enemy; the fully supported mode |
| `single_ally` | one living ally, never the actor |
| `self` | the actor |
| `team_enemy` | every living enemy |
| `team_ally` | every living ally, actor included |
| `team_all` | every living combatant on both sides, actor included |
| `single_pc` | the player character |

Use the ordinary condition gate to narrow `single_ally` by target state. For
example, Tongue of Beasts requires the selected ally to be in PoD's Wolf Form:

```paradox
POD_combat_move_set_condition = {
	MODE = gate
	TARGET = target
	PREDICATE = has_modifier
	THRESHOLD = 0
}
POD_combat_move_set_cond_param = { PARAM = pod_shapeshift_form_wolf_modifier }
```

Player validation and AI ally selection both check the authored modifier
gate. Use `has_modifier` for a `single_ally` target gate.

### Broadcast support

| Payload | single_enemy | single_ally | self | team_enemy | team_ally | team_all |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| `hp_damage` | yes | to the enemy | to the enemy | yes | to the enemy | yes, actor included |
| `morale_damage` | yes | to the enemy | to the enemy | yes | to the enemy | yes, actor included |
| `hp_heal` / `morale_heal` | yes | to the ally | to the actor | to the actor | yes | no arm exists |
| `energy_gain` | to the actor | to the actor | to the actor | to the actor | to the actor | to the actor |
| soak/hit **buff** tiers | to the actor | to the ally | to the actor | to the actor | yes | no arm exists |
| soak/hit **debuff** tiers | yes | to the ally | to the enemy | yes | no | yes, actor included |
| `set_guard` / `dodge` / `stealth` | to the actor | to the ally | to the actor | to the actor | yes | no arm exists |
| `bypass_dodge` / `bypass_stealth` / `remove_guard` | yes | - | - | yes | no | yes, never self-applied |
| DoT, `mind_control`, `ap_drain`, `initiative_debuff`, `steal_gold` | yes | - | - | **one target only** | **one target only** | **one target only** |
| every non-actor-side bonus effect | yes | - | - | **one target only** | **one target only** | **one target only** |
| retaliation **arming** | yes | yes | yes | yes | yes | yes |
| triggers the victim's armed counter | if it deals HP damage | - | if it deals HP damage | never | - | never |
| `marker_modifier` | actor | actor | actor | actor | actor | actor |
| `remove_marker` (target=user) | actor | actor | actor | actor | actor | actor |
| `remove_marker` (target=target) | enemy | ally | rejected | rejected | rejected | rejected |

`single_pc` redirects **heals only**. Buff tiers and stances test
`single_ally` exclusively, so on a `single_pc` move they land on the caster.
Use `single_ally` if a buff must reach the beneficiary.

`self` has no damage arm of its own, so `hp_damage` on a `self` move still
routes to the selected enemy. Use `set_self_damage` to damage the actor.

On `team_all` the caster takes the move's own HP and morale damage, classified
by its damage class. The HP share bypasses guard and the hit roll; the morale
share does not, so a caster in Dodge or Stealth consumes that stance and takes
no morale from its own blast.

A team-targeted move whose **entire** payload is utility is subject to a
separate admissibility gate (section 20).

