## 8. Presence flags: the complete set

Every flag is written the same way:

```paradox
POD_combat_move_set_flag = { NAME = <flag> }
```

Only these flag names are read at runtime.

| Flag | Effect |
|---|---|
| `requires_hit_roll` | delivery: roll to hit (section 6) |
| `checks_guard` | delivery: Guard can block |
| `checks_stance` | delivery: Dodge and Stealth can evade |
| `checks_spirit_gate` | delivery: physical spirit gate applies |
| `requires_control_contact` | a payload-free move must land to apply its control effects |
| `bypass_dodge` | strip and ignore the target's Dodge |
| `bypass_stealth` | break and ignore the target's Stealth |
| `set_guard` | apply Guard. Blocks the next incoming move that checks guard, then is consumed |
| `dodge` | apply the Dodge stance |
| `stealth` | apply the Stealth stance, plus a hit bonus (30 by default) while it lasts |
| `remove_guard` | strip Guard from the hostile target, for later attackers too |
| `mind_control` | steal the target's next AI turn unless its mental defenses resist. Players are immune |
| `drain` | mark a damage-plus-heal move as a drain, for presentation and AI understanding |
| `dot_morale` | the move's damage-over-time ticks hit morale instead of HP |
| `retaliate_if_hit` | arm a counter that fires on an incoming HP-damage move that makes contact |
| `retaliate_if_missed` | arm a counter that fires when an incoming HP-damage move misses or is evaded |
| `retaliate_if_attacked` | arm one counter that answers either outcome |
| `summon_hostile` | seat the summoned creature on the side opposite the caster |
| `is_starter_move` | include the move in default player loadout seeding |
| `uses_weapon` | apply the equipped weapon's damage retype, bonus damage, dodge bypass and aggravated overrides. Excludes natural weapons and conjured blades. For conditional use, omit this flag and add a `uses_weapon` clause (section 16) |

Starter seeding does not check unlock rules; runtime access still does.
Non-starters get an AI class-repertoire weight bonus.

Use `single_enemy` for `mind_control`; other targeting modes receive no
mind-control AI weight.

`retaliate_agg`, `retaliate_morale`, `summons_combatant`, `summon_recipe` and
`marker_modifier` look like flags but have their own setters. See sections
11, 13 and 17.

