## 15. Conditions

A move may have one **gate** and any number of **bonus clauses** (section 16).

```paradox
POD_combat_move_set_condition = {
    MODE      = gate
    TARGET    = target
    PREDICATE = hp_missing
    THRESHOLD = 2
}
```

| Parameter | Values |
|---|---|
| `MODE` | `gate` (move unusable while false) |
| `TARGET` | `user`, `target`, `global`, `relational` |
| `PREDICATE` | one of the conditions below |
| `THRESHOLD` | the number for numeric conditions; pass `0` for boolean ones |

Bonus conditions and effects belong to clause stories. The `if+` display
reads the move's `bonus_clauses` list. Use `POD_combat_move_set_condition`
for the move gate.

For conditional AP drain, also set
`POD_combat_move_set_sheet_ap_drain = { VALUE = n }` to the sum of all
`ap_drain` clauses. The sheet AP column and compact line read this display
value from the move story; execution reads the clauses.

### Conditions

| Condition | `TARGET` | `THRESHOLD` |
|---|---|---|
| `first_round` | `global` | 0 |
| `round_min` | `global` | minimum round |
| `outnumbered` | `global` | 0 |
| `ally_knocked_out` | `global` | 0 |
| `alive_enemies_min` | `global` | minimum living enemies |
| `alive_enemies_max` | `global` | maximum living enemies |
| `alive_allies_min` | `global` | minimum living allies **excluding the actor** |
| `alive_allies_max` | `global` | maximum living allies **excluding the actor** (0 = last one standing) |
| `undamaged` | `user` or `target` | 0 |
| `hp_missing` | `user` or `target` | minimum wound boxes filled |
| `full_morale` | `user` or `target` | 0 |
| `morale_missing` | `user` or `target` | minimum morale lost |
| `has_guard` | `user` or `target` | 0 |
| `has_dodge` | `user` or `target` | 0 |
| `has_stealth` | `user` or `target` | 0 |
| `prestige_level_min` | `user` or `target` | 0-5 |
| `piety_level_min` | `user` or `target` | 0-5 |
| `dread_min` | `user` or `target` | 0-100 |
| `has_weapon_artifact` | `user` or `target` | 0 |
| `has_armor_artifact` | `user` or `target` | 0 |
| `relation_positive` | `relational` | minimum opinion |
| `relation_negative` | `relational` | minimum opinion magnitude, as a positive number |
| `has_trait` | `user` or `target` | 0, plus `PARAM` |
| `has_modifier` | `user` or `target` | 0, plus `PARAM` |
| `has_perk` | `user` or `target` | 0, plus `PARAM` |
| `fera_form` | `user` or `target` | 0, plus `PARAM` |
| `target_known_secret` | `relational` | 0, plus `PARAM` |
| `wyrm_servant` | `user` or `target` | 0 |
| `is_fera` | `user` or `target` | 0 |

Choose thresholds deliberately. A zero minimum often makes a condition
unconditional; `alive_allies_max` with `THRESHOLD = 0` requires no surviving allies.

`target_known_secret` uses `pod_combat_cond_known_secret_trigger`, which
always returns false. Do not use this condition.

### Identifier conditions

`has_modifier`, `has_perk` and `fera_form` resolve literal keys through
`common/scripted_triggers/POD_combat/pod_combat_condition_dispatch_triggers.txt`.
Each key needs a matching switch case in its scripted trigger.

```paradox
POD_combat_move_set_cond_param        = { PARAM = cobra_fangs_perk }   # the gate
POD_combat_move_clause_set_cond_param = { PARAM = cobra_fangs_perk }   # a bonus clause
```

| Condition | Supported keys | What a key may be |
|---|---|---|
| `has_perk` | perk keys listed in the scripted trigger | any perk in PoD's `lifestyle_perks` |
| `fera_form` | `primalhuman`, `warform`, `primalbeast`, `beast` | `primalhuman`, `warform`, `primalbeast`, `beast` |
| `has_modifier` | the five `archid_*_modifier` keys, `pod_shapeshift_form_wolf_modifier`, plus `pod_combat_anima_flare`, `pod_combat_predator_focus`, `pod_combat_kai_focus`, and `comrades_at_arms_wind_dance_modifier` | a modifier key with a scripted-trigger switch case |
| `target_known_secret` | none (fail-closed stub) | any secret_type |

A new literal flag may also need a row in
`pod_combat_error_suppression_effects.txt`, but only after spelling, scope and
real runtime use are verified.

Trait conditions are set with a different scripted effect, by passing the trait scope:

```paradox
POD_combat_move_set_cond_param_trait        = { PARAM = trait:vampire }   # the gate
POD_combat_move_clause_set_cond_param_trait = { PARAM = trait:vampire }   # a bonus clause
```

