## 16. Bonus clauses and their effects

Each bonus clause has its own condition and effect. Fulfilled clauses apply
together: magnitudes sum, while tier effects use the highest tier.

```paradox
POD_combat_move_add_bonus_clause = {
    TARGET    = target
    PREDICATE = has_perk
    THRESHOLD = 0
    EFFECT    = energy_drain
    VALUE     = 2
}
POD_combat_move_clause_set_cond_param = { PARAM = cobra_fangs_perk }
```

Supply `TARGET`, `PREDICATE`, `THRESHOLD`, `EFFECT` and `VALUE` on each
`POD_combat_move_add_bonus_clause` call. Optional parameters use
`POD_combat_move_clause_set_cond_param`,
`POD_combat_move_clause_set_bonus_param` and
`POD_combat_move_clause_set_hide`. Keep these setters immediately after their
clause constructor: they modify the most recently created clause.

| `EFFECT` | `VALUE` means | Compatible with |
|---|---|---|
| `damage` | extra HP damage; blank `bonus_param` joins the main packet, a class routes a separate typed packet | a move with an HP damage path |
| `morale_damage` | extra morale damage | a hostile target |
| `change_type` | pass `0`; forces this hit aggravated | a move with HP damage |
| `hit` | added hit chance, recapped at 95 | a move that rolls to hit; **wiped on any team move** |
| `self_heal` | HP restored to the actor | anything |
| `heal_target` | HP restored to the selected target | single target only |
| `ap_refund` | AP returned to the actor | must stay strictly below `AP_COST` |
| `ap_drain` | AP removed from the selected target, next turn | `single_enemy` only, `VALUE` at least 1; sums with base `ap_drain` |
| `stance_guard` | pass `0` | the actor only |
| `stance_dodge` | pass `0` | the actor only |
| `stance_stealth` | pass `0` | the actor only |
| `energy_gain` | energy restored to the actor | anything |
| `energy_drain` | energy removed from the selected target | single target only |
| `dot` | damage per tick, fixed 2 rounds | `single_enemy` only; never alongside a base DoT (one slot, the second erases the first) |
| `morale_dot` | morale per tick, fixed 2 rounds | as `dot`; damages morale and uses the morale affliction log row |
| `self_morale_heal` | morale restored to the actor | the actor only |
| `retaliate_boost` | damage added to the counter this move arms | requires a `retaliate_if_*` flag; boosts every family the move arms |
| `uses_weapon` | pass `0`; grants the weapon swing for this action | a move with an HP damage path, typed DoT or typed counter; never alongside the static `uses_weapon` flag |
| `change_class` | pass `0`; the element goes in `bonus_param` | a move with no authored `damage_type`, an HP/DoT/counter consumer, not Mental, not statically `uses_weapon` |
| `hit_buff_round` | pass the TIER (1-3); hit-chance tier to the recipient, one round | never `team*`; not alongside a base tier of the same stat/direction/duration |
| `hit_debuff_round` | pass the TIER (1-3); costs the target a hit-chance tier, one round | `single_enemy` only; same base-tier restriction |
| `soak_buff_round` | pass the TIER (1-3); soak tier to the recipient, one round | never `team*`; same base-tier restriction |
| `soak_debuff_round` | pass the TIER (1-3); costs the target a soak tier, one round | `single_enemy` only; same base-tier restriction |
| `hit_buff_combat` | as `hit_buff_round`, for the rest of combat | never `team*`; same base-tier restriction |
| `hit_debuff_combat` | as `hit_debuff_round`, for the rest of combat | `single_enemy` only; same base-tier restriction |
| `soak_buff_combat` | as `soak_buff_round`, for the rest of combat | never `team*`; same base-tier restriction |
| `soak_debuff_combat` | as `soak_debuff_round`, for the rest of combat | `single_enemy` only; same base-tier restriction |

`change_type`, `change_class`, `uses_weapon` and `stance_*` ignore `VALUE`;
pass `0`. Tier effects take `VALUE = 1`, `2` or `3` (small, medium or large);
fulfilled clauses of the same effect use the highest tier.

Set `bonus_param` with `POD_combat_move_clause_set_bonus_param` for:

- `change_class`: one of the ten elements, converting the main packet.
- `damage`: `superficial`, `aggravated` or an element, applying a separate
  wound packet with `VALUE` at least 1. Omit the parameter to add damage to
  the main packet. Typed clauses sum per class, with up to three classes per
  move, each logged separately in class-table order.

The sum of all `ap_refund` clauses must remain below `AP_COST`. Include this
sum when checking for repeatable net-positive AP.

### Clause exclusivity (never legal)

| Rejected pairing | Why |
|---|---|
| `change_type` + `change_class` | execution section 6 applies aggravated first, making conversion unreachable |
| `dot` + `morale_dot` | both write the same DoT slot; the second overwrites the first |
| `uses_weapon` clause + `change_class` clause | both change the action's damage class |
| the same magnitude-less effect twice | nothing to sum; the three `stance_*` are the exception and coexist |

`uses_weapon` and `ap_drain` may appear in any clause position. Neither may
be hidden: the weapon tag reads all clauses and the AP column displays their
summed drain.

### The `hide` flag

```paradox
POD_combat_move_clause_set_hide = yes
```

Hides the clause's condition and effect lines until the viewer meets its
condition. Only `user`-targeted `has_perk`, `has_trait` and `has_modifier`
clauses support hiding; `ap_drain` and `uses_weapon` cannot be hidden.
The `if+` glyph and compact "bonus if..." text still indicate a conditional
bonus. The `notes` line is always visible, so it must not disclose hidden
effects.

A `uses_weapon` clause enables equipped `primary_armament` overrides for this
action. Execution sections 2c and 6 read it through
`pod_combat_move_swings_weapon_trigger`.

Affordability checks use gross `ap_cost` before refunds. The actor must afford
that amount, and runtime does not clamp the refund below it.

A bonus should reward a distinct state, not reproduce the base payload every
use.

