## 17. Marker modifiers

```paradox
POD_combat_move_set_marker_modifier = { KEY = pod_combat_anima_flare }
```

A marker lets later actions test move-applied state with `has_modifier`. An
`ap_refund` clause can use it to reduce those actions' net AP cost.

Keys are defined in `common/modifiers/pod_combat_modifiers.txt`. The live keys
are `pod_combat_anima_flare`, `pod_combat_predator_focus`, and
`pod_combat_kai_focus`.

- Markers always apply to the actor, regardless of targeting.
- Conditions resolve in execution section 2b; markers apply in 12c. A newly
  applied marker cannot satisfy a condition on that same action.
- A marker condition uses one bonus clause, leaving the gate and other clauses
  available.
- Markers persist across rounds. Teardown and slot seating remove them;
  `days = 30` limits persistence if cleanup fails.

Adding a key touches: the modifier block and its name/`_desc` loc, the section
12c apply switch, the 12b-marker strip switch, the `has_modifier` scripted
trigger, and three removal sites
(`pod_combat_duel_end_effect`, `pod_combat_host_died_release_effect`, and
slot initialization). Keep these sites consistent.

